From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:10:00 +0200
Subject: media: rkvdec: Leave the clocks to runtime PM

Since commit 6a846f7d72c7 ("media: rkvdec: Enable all clocks without
naming them") the clocks are fetched with devm_clk_bulk_get_all_enabled(),
which keeps them enabled from probe until unbind. Runtime PM enables and
disables them on top of that, so their enable count never drops to zero
and the clocks stay ungated while the decoder is idle.

On RK3399 this also breaks restore from hibernation: the restored kernel
counts the vdu clocks as enabled while they are gated in hardware, and
it hangs on the first write to the vdu QoS registers when the vdu power
domain is powered on.

Get the clocks without enabling them and let runtime PM enable them
while the decoder is in use, as before that commit.

Fixes: 6a846f7d72c7 ("media: rkvdec: Enable all clocks without naming them")
Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1851,7 +1851,7 @@ static int rkvdec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

-	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all_enabled(&pdev->dev, &rkvdec->clocks);
+	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(&pdev->dev, &rkvdec->clocks);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;

